{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786650131515107002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"albinic-agrologic-dolphin","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"fe47c8d0c3733352a2d04ece5e267b0486fce18b47c9586a26714670a9c4218f","event_uuid":"fef84a97-f915-4a10-a662-de95875f99e2","position":{"commit_sha":"ef5b43e5abda64898bc95ab62273297f55a7742d","position":"1786650105971258001-fef84a97-f915-4a10-a662-de95875f99e2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0bc6ba023bff964c1295eb5d664177db4c439dd2e9c76b77d90af6dd550883d7","event_uuid":"37adfab1-bb91-43f3-a63b-1053c66e888c","position":{"commit_sha":"528b58b991d47b95f64003a233041442aad24446","position":"1786650131515107001-37adfab1-bb91-43f3-a63b-1053c66e888c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786650105971258001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"37adfab1-bb91-43f3-a63b-1053c66e888c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ce7d-3a15-51e5-4c6a"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nOn the Gerrit `Verified` gate, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py::test_rendered_output_is_byte_identical_to_the_landed_renderer` intermittently CRASHES its pytest-xdist worker instead of failing an assertion:\n\n```\nworker 'gw1' crashed while running\n  tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py::test_rendered_output_is_byte_identical_to_the_landed_renderer\n1 failed, 12849 passed, 65 skipped in 1664.64s (0:27:44)\n```\n\nObserved 2026-08-13 on run 31734135055 (change 1731, patchset 2), macos-latest/py3.13 ONLY — the three ubuntu cells passed. There is no traceback and no assertion text, so the whole matrix job reds and the change takes a `Verified -1` it did not earn.\n\n## Why this is not the already-tracked xdist flake\n`c89f-08b1-2e8c-4133` and `fade-ea90-7564-4715` (both closed) cover the same *shape* — an xdist worker dying with no traceback — but on `tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py::test_matching_guard_is_accepted`, a different test with a different cause. This is the wiki-render variant and has no ticket of its own.\n\n## Leading hypothesis (not yet confirmed)\nThe test drives pandoc subprocesses over a corpus and compares rendered output byte-for-byte. Story `271c-e88f-3220-4c9b` recorded exactly this failure mode for a sibling wiki-render test in its ps3 note: the multi-pass corpus test exceeded CI's 300s per-test timeout on the contended macOS lane, and the worker died rather than reporting. macOS runners are the scarcest cell in the org-wide pool (5 concurrent), so contention there is routine. If that is the cause, the fix is about the test's per-unit cost or its timeout budget, not about the renderer.\n\nThis is a hypothesis from the run metadata plus a documented sibling, NOT a confirmed root cause. It needs the `/rebar-debug` treatment: reproduce deterministically (a contended macOS lane, or the per-test timeout lowered locally until it reproduces), confirm the mechanism, then fix the class.\n\n## Evidence it is not caused by the change that surfaced it\n- Change 1734 contains 1731's exact commit plus one more and passed macos-latest/py3.13 with identical renderer code.\n- 1731 touches five files, none runtime: the portability rubric, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and two portability test modules.\n- The full unit suite passed locally on that tree: 12853 passed, 0 failed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The crash is reproduced deterministically and the mechanism named (timeout budget vs. an actual renderer/subprocess fault), with the reproduction recorded here.\n- [ ] The class is fixed, not the instance — if the cause is the per-test budget on a contended lane, every wiki-render test sharing that shape is covered by the same fix.\n- [ ] A `Verified` run on the fixed suite passes the macOS cell, and the fix does not weaken the byte-identity property the test exists to protect.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0078-fa3e-05d1-4e12","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Flaky CI: wiki-render hardening test kills its xdist worker on macOS","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["fef84a97-f915-4a10-a662-de95875f99e2","37adfab1-bb91-43f3-a63b-1053c66e888c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786650131515107002,"uuid":"de77a041-8a76-44b8-96a6-087699ff6790"}